## 7. SHOPPING CART

Implement a functional shopping cart.

Allow both anonymous visitors and authenticated users to add products to their carts.

### Anonymous cart
- Store cart information in the Django session.
- Do not require login just to add products.
- Preserve the cart while the session remains valid.

### Authenticated cart
- Persist cart data in the database.
- Allow customers to view their saved cart across authenticated sessions.

### Cart features
- Add products.
- Remove products.
- Increase quantity.
- Decrease quantity.
- Validate available stock.
- Display product subtotal.
- Display total item count.
- Calculate the cart subtotal.
- Display shipping charges where applicable.
- Calculate applicable discounts.
- Calculate the final payable amount.
- Display an empty-cart page when no items exist.

### Cart merging

When an anonymous visitor logs in:
- Merge the session cart with the authenticated customer's cart.
- Combine matching product quantities where appropriate.
- Revalidate current product availability and stock.
- Avoid exceeding available inventory.
- Notify the customer if a cart item is no longer available.

Calculate all prices on the server using current database values. Never trust prices submitted by the browser.

